# Local/emulator overrides for `wrangler dev` (copy to .dev.vars — gitignored).
#
# Production uses real Firebase JWT verification + Firestore over HTTPS and does
# NOT need any of these. For local runs against your Firebase emulator:

# Accept unsigned emulator ID tokens (no JWKS round-trip).
AUTH_MODE = "firebase_emulator"

# Point Firestore reads at your local emulator (membership gate reads
# teams/{teamId}). Adjust host/port to your setup.
FIRESTORE_REST_BASE = "http://127.0.0.1:8080"

# Project id (matches the data-plane / app). Already set in wrangler.toml [vars]
# for production; override here only if your emulator uses a different id.
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID = "maiplayer-ac56d"

# NOTE: this worker needs NO secrets in production. The relay fallback travels
# over the WebSocket through the DO (see RelayMessage in types.ts) — there is no
# RTDB/service-account path, so FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL / FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY /
# FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL are not used.
